#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1300 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "The positive control for the wave-15 `dataset_domain` migration on `PMDA-SD1300`. Every row carries the three-character `DOMAIN` value `LBX`; `dataset_domain` (`OperationExecutor.unsplitNameFromData`) reads the ROW-0 cell verbatim and does not normalise, so `longer_than 2` fires and `Sensitivity: Dataset` collapses it to one dataset-level finding. ⚑ Added because the migration would otherwise ship UNEXERCISED — `PMDA-SD1300` had no scenario at all before wave 15. ⚠ The anchor row is deliberately not pinned: `dataset_domain` is a dataset constant, so the anchor carries no information."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
---
S1 | LBX | 001 | 1
S1 | LBX | 001 | 2
---
